      "widgets_values": [
        "How the reference pictures align with the target video — Picture 1 (from Shot 1) aligns with the 0.00-second mark of the target video; Picture 2 (from Shot 1) aligns with the 10.13-second mark of the target video.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] This is a live-action, cinematic shot. A young woman in a long black dress stands on a wet, rain-slicked street at night, holding a black umbrella over her head. The background is a vibrant cityscape with glowing neon signs and blurred pedestrians. Early in the clip, she takes a slow, deliberate step forward, her gaze fixed on the illuminated interior of the nearby coffee shop. As she approaches the glass door, she lowers her arms, carefully folding the umbrella and setting it down on the wet pavement. The camera pushes in and trucks right, smoothly transitioning from the exterior street view to the interior of the cozy café. Inside, the woman steps up to a large window, her dark hair catching the warm, golden light spilling from the interior. She gracefully lowers herself onto a brown leather chair, her posture relaxed. Toward the end of the clip, she reaches out with both hands to grasp a white ceramic coffee cup resting on a saucer, lifting it slightly as she settles into her final seated position, looking out thoughtfully at the rainy street.\n\noverall_soundscape: The soundscape begins with the steady, rhythmic patter of rain hitting the pavement and the woman's umbrella, layered over the distant, muffled hum of city traffic. As she moves, the wet, squelching sound of her footsteps on the slick ground is clearly heard. This is followed by a distinct, sharp click as the umbrella is folded and set down on the pavement. The moment she enters the café, the ambient noise shifts to the warm, comforting room tone of the interior, accompanied by the faint, indistinct murmur of other patrons. A subtle rustle of her dress fabric is audible as she sits down, ending with a soft, distinct clink as she grasps the ceramic coffee cup.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A slow, atmospheric jazz track featuring a gentle piano melody and a soft upright bass plays throughout, enhancing the moody and cinematic feel of the rainy night."
